  compatibility for published APIs, external consumers, durable data, rolling migrations, or user
  requirements. Name the consumer and removal condition; avoid hypothetical compatibility.
- Keep framework primitives visible; prefer duplication over premature wrappers. Let TypeScript
  expose breakage and fail loudly on unexpected input.
